# Gate captain of the southern wall. Fighter route into chapter 1:
# intimidate him (Hard) for the mansion's whereabouts, or kill him and loot his gate log.

%rec: OpeningBranch

cond: IsActorInCombatWithPlayer(NPC)
goto: PlayerCombatBranch

cond: HasFlag('LocationKnown(mansion)')
goto: AlreadyTold

cond: true
goto: DefaultIntroduction

%rec: Nodes

name: PlayerCombatBranch
npc: You picked the wrong gate, contractor.
effect: EndConversation

name: AlreadyTold
npc: You know the way. Don't make me regret it.
effect: EndConversation

name: DefaultIntroduction
npc: Gate's closed to foot traffic. State your business or move along.
#
o_text: Trucks have been going out this gate at night. Where to?
o_id: ask_trucks
o_goto: AskTrucks
#
o_text: Nothing. Just looking.
o_id: leave
o_goto: Bye

name: AskTrucks
npc: (He doesn't blink.) Outbound traffic is logged, not discussed.
#
o_text: Then I'll take it off your corpse. Your call.
o_id: intimidate
o_test: RollSkill('intimidate', 'Hard')
o_succ: IntimidateSuccess
o_fail: IntimidateFail
#
o_text: Fair enough.
o_goto: Bye

name: IntimidateSuccess
npc: (He glances at the empty yard, then lowers his voice.)
+ Private residence. Old highway, half an hour south. Caterers, security, the lot.
+ You got that from nobody. Now get off my gate.
effect: SetFlag('LocationKnown(mansion)')
effect: EndConversation

name: IntimidateFail
npc: (He rests a hand on his holster.) Try me. Go on.
#
o_text: <Fight>
o_id: fight
o_goto: Fight
#
o_text: Another time.
o_goto: Bye

name: Fight
npc: Thought so.
effect: StartCombat

name: Bye
npc: Move along.
effect: EndConversation
